                  <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Steps:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ol style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Load &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;normalized &lt;/span&gt;WASSR file.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Load WASSR offsets.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Type valid filename and save images.  Three images will be saved: &lt;br/&gt;a. *_fitted (fitted curve)&lt;br/&gt;b. *_fitted_params (fit parameters)&lt;br/&gt;c. *_dB0 (∆B0 map)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;p&gt;This widget fits the WASSR image with a single Gaussian peak.  It then uses the shift of the peak to estimate the ∆B0 (offset from 0 ppm).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
